epics.description:
**Observed (2026-09-06, main @ 0484bdf)**

`lib/claude/spawn.ts:376-388` (and the streaming variant at `:652-661`):

```ts
const kill = () => {
  if (child && !child.killed) {
    killed = true;
    child.kill("SIGTERM");
    setTimeout(() => {
      if (child && !child.killed) {   // always false after kill()
        child.kill("SIGKILL");
      }
    }, 5000);
  }
};
```

Node sets `child.killed = true` as soon as the SIGTERM is *delivered*, before the process exits. Measured on Node v22.22.3: right after `kill('SIGTERM')`, `killed=true`, `exitCode=null`, `signalCode=null`. So the escalation is dead code. The spawn at `:286-290` is also not `detached: true`, so only the head `claude` process is ever signalled; subshells, test runners and dev servers it started survive.

`lib/providers/base-provider.ts:616-634` already fixed exactly this for codex/omp/agy (guard on `exitCode`/`signalCode`, `detached: true`, signal `-pid`) and documents the symptom: "a session marked `cancelled` in the database kept writing to a worktree that a live session had meanwhile been handed". The claude-code path (`lib/providers/claude-code.ts:54` → `spawnClaude`) does not go through it.

**Failure scenario under Full Auto:** DELETE session → `processManager.cancel()` sends SIGTERM and flips status to `cancelled` synchronously → launch closure returns at once → `holdFailedBuild` pulls the ticket to `in_progress` → terminal hook kicks a sweep 250 ms later → a fresh build is dispatched into the **same worktree** while the SIGTERM'd claude tree may still be editing it.

**Expected**
- Extract `isChildAlive` / `signalChild` from base-provider into a shared module and use them in `spawnClaude` and `spawnClaudeStream`; spawn `detached: true` and signal `-pid`.
- Have the closure wait for the actual `close` event (or a bounded grace) before `holdFailedBuild` runs.

Related (same audit): no PID/PGID is persisted on `agent_sessions`, so `failOrphanedRunningSessions` (`lib/agent-sessions/boot-cleanup.ts:106-135`) cannot kill agents orphaned by a server restart; its docstring's claim that children die with the server is false on Linux (and codex/omp/agy are `detached`). Also `instrumentation.ts` runs the boot sweep (lines 52-53) *before* `setSessionTerminalHook` (line 77), so restart orphans never get the failure notification.

Found by the 2026-09-06 tech check (concurrency section).

## Latent, not reachable from any current mount

Found while fixing Za4qnzacwCrq (the uncontrolled→controlled warning). Reproduced on the base tree **and** on the fixed tree, so it is pre-existing and independent of that fix. None of the eight mounts of `components/shared/NamedAgentSelect.tsx` (`RefinementDialog`, `NightRunDialog`, `AutoModeDialog` ×2, `StartQaCheckDialog`, `ChangelogAgentPopover`, `AgentDispatchDialog`, the git-sync page, the project desk page) sits inside a `<form>`, which is the only place it fires — filed so the next mount inside a form does not rediscover it.

## Mechanism (Radix `@radix-ui/react-select` 2.2.6)

`Select.Root` renders a visually hidden native `<select>` (`SelectBubbleInput`) whenever `trigger.closest("form")` is truthy. When the controlled `value` changes, that input's effect assigns the new value to the native select and dispatches a `change` event. At the moment the agent list loads, the picker's value goes from the loading placeholder to the preselected id **in the same commit** that mounts the `SelectContent` — but the native `<option>`s are only registered by the items' effects one render later. The native select therefore has no matching option, reads back `""`, and Radix's `onChange={(e) => setValue(e.target.value)}` forwards that `""` to `onValueChange`, which the picker passes to the parent as `onChange("")`. A parent that stores it wipes its preselected agent right after the list arrives.

## Reproduction (vitest, jsdom, real Radix Select)

```tsx
let resolve!: (a: unknown[]) => void;
const answer = new Promise<unknown[]>((r) => { resolve = r; });
vi.stubGlobal("fetch", vi.fn(async () => ({ ok: true, status: 200, json: async () => ({ data: await answer }) })));
const onChange = vi.fn();
render(<form><NamedAgentSelect value="agent-1" onChange={onChange} aria-label="Agent" /></form>);
await act(async () => {
  resolve([{ id: "agent-1", name: "Claude Code", provider: "claude-code", model: "opus" }]);
  await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 0));
});
// observed: onChange.mock.calls === [[""]]  (base tree and fixed tree alike)
// without the <form> wrapper: onChange is never called (pinned by __tests__/named-agent-select-controlled.test.tsx)
```

## Suggested fix

Radix never emits `""` for a user action: `SelectItem` forbids an empty value and the picker's clear row is the `__none__` sentinel. So in `NamedAgentSelect`'s `onValueChange`, an empty `next` can only be this bubble-input echo and can be dropped (`if (next === "") return;`) — with a comment saying why, and a test that renders the picker inside a `<form>` and asserts `onChange` stays silent across the load. Alternatively keep the picker on the empty-string value until the items have registered, but that is a second render pass for no visible gain.

Adjacent finding from the review of the ToastStack migration on `/projects/:id/github-issues` (commit `4d72ef16`). Pre-existing, introduced by `9526feb2`, untouched by that migration and non-blocking for it.

`saveMappingConfig` in `app/projects/[projectId]/github-issues/page.tsx:156-175` fires a `PUT /api/projects/:id/github/label-mapping` and does nothing with the result:

```ts
async function saveMappingConfig() {
  setSavingMapping(true);
  try {
    await fetch(`/api/projects/${projectId}/github/label-mapping`, { method: "PUT", ... });
  } finally {
    setSavingMapping(false);
  }
}
```

Three defects in one:

1. **No `res.ok` check.** A 4xx/5xx from the route is indistinguishable from a success: the spinner stops and the panel looks saved. The mapping decides which imported issues become feature epics and which become bugs, so a silently-dropped save is a wrong classification later.
2. **No success feedback either.** The page now has a working `ToastStack`, and the two other write paths on the same screen (`syncNow`, `importSelected`) both raise on success and on failure. This one is the odd surface out.
3. **Unhandled promise rejection.** The handler is wired as `onClick={saveMappingConfig}` (line 468), and there is no `catch` — only a `finally`. A network failure rejects a promise nobody awaits.

The review ticket's own suggested reproduction was "trigger an action that calls showToast (e.g. save mapping)", which cannot be followed: save mapping raises no toast at all, before or after the migration.

## Suggested fix

Mirror `syncNow`: branch on `res.ok`, `showToast("error", json.error || t(...))` on failure, `showToast("success", t(...))` on success, and wrap in `try/catch/finally`. Two new catalogue keys under `GithubIssues.mapping` (`savedToast`, `saveFailed`) and their `fr` seeds. A component test belongs in `__tests__/github-issues-page-labels.test.tsx`, which already renders this panel.

## Verification state

Read from source; no browser reproduction. `npx tsc --noEmit` and `eslint` are clean on the file as it stands.

